Privacy Policy for SafeИщчЗдгы
Last updated: November 19, 2026
1. Overview
Safebox Syncer ("the App") is a utility plugin designed exclusively to synchronize encrypted backup files created by the Safe+ password manager with cloud storage providers selected by the user (Google Drive, Dropbox, Box.com, Yandex.Disk, and FTP/FTPS servers).
2. Data Collection and Storage
• No External Servers: The App does not operate any developer-owned backend servers. All file transfers occur directly between your Android device and your personal cloud storage account.
• No Personal Data Collection: We do not collect, track, store, or share your personal information, contacts, passwords, or analytics.
• Encrypted Files Only: The App only reads and uploads encrypted database files located in the mySafeboxPro directory. The App cannot decrypt or view the contents of your database.
3. Google Drive API Services User Data Policy
Safebox Syncer's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements:
• Scope of Access: The App requests access to Google Drive solely to create, read, update, and delete your encrypted backup files inside the mySafeboxPro folder.
• Local Token Storage: OAuth access and refresh tokens are stored strictly locally in your device's private application preferences (SharedPreferences) and are never transmitted to any third party.
• Revoking Access: You can disconnect your Google account at any time inside the App or by revoking access in your Google Account security settings.
